f99d0a9afa2864db2d" "basis" 1173 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-16380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-10{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}+20x+36y=64?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}+20x+36y & =64 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+36y-10{x}^{2}+20x & =64 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}+4y]-10[{x}^{2}-2x] & =64 \\\\ 9[(y+2)^{2}-4]-10[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =64 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-36-10(x-1)^{2}+10 & =64 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-10(x-1)^{2} & =64+36-10 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-10(x-1)^{2} & =90 \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(1,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65adc7a66836036a0debf372f02c0bf1418db5b74d85a5b9d4821c1acfe0bacf"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,-1)"] ["math" "(-2,-2)"] ["math" "(-2,1)"] ["math" "(1,-2)"] ["math" "(2,-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-78358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{7}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-78358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{7}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=3$ and $k=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(3,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-78358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65adc7a66836036a0debf372f02c0bf1418db5b74d85a5b9d4821c1acfe0bacf"} {"question" "q-78358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-78358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,3)"] ["math" "(-3,2)"] ["math" "(2,-3)"] ["math" "(3,-2)"] ["math" "(3,2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-78358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,-2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n${x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}+6x+48y=71?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}+6x+48y & =71 \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x-8{y}^{2}+48y & =71 \\\\ [{x}^{2}+6x]-8[{y}^{2}-6y] & =71 \\\\ [(x+3)^{2}-9]-8[(y-3)^{2}-9] & =71 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-9-8(y-3)^{2}+72 & =71 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-8(y-3)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{8}-(y-3)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-3,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65adc7a66836036a0debf372f02c0bf1418db5b74d85a5b9d4821c1acfe0bacf"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,3)"] ["math" "(1,-8)"] ["math" "(3,-3)"] ["math" "(3,3)"] ["math" "(8,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-3,3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-328353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-12x+16y=28$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-328353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-12x+16y & =28 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-12x-4{y}^{2}+16y & =28 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-4x]-4[{y}^{2}-4y] & =28 \\\\ 3[(x-2)^{2}-4]-4[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =28 \\\\ 3(x-2)^{2}-12-4(y-2)^{2}+16 & =28 \\\\ 3(x-2)^{2}-4(y-2)^{2} & =28+12-16 \\\\ 3(x-2)^{2}-4(y-2)^{2} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,2,2\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065191/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e8c197365cf0eeffe3540e58e2373e50f0283d2dc3e65fcd9e8c0556a62523e"} {"question" "q-328353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Dev